   "financial_implications": "See report",
   "action": "Action: M/S/C (Tregub/Lunaparra) to accept revised material from Councilmember Tregub on Item 20. Vote: All Ayes. Action: 17 speakers. M/S/C (Taplin/O’Keefe) to 1) adopt the first reading of Ordinance No. 8,005–N.S. as proposed by staff and incorporating the alternatives proposed by Councilmember Kesarwani; further amended as noted below: • Add language in Supplemental Communications Packet #2 from Councilmember Humbert regarding the 5-year term and other SB 330 provisions. • Include new language from at the meeting to add paragraph 3. under 3.24.120(C) to read “If the property owner submits a formal zoning application for a wholly non-residential project on the subject property during the 5-year exception period, the exception period shall immediately terminate and the processing of any landmark designation may resume.” • Amended to apply a 200-signature threshold in all circumstances 2) request a report from the City Manager in one year regarding the implementation of the new regulations. Second reading scheduled for April 28, 2026. Vote: Ayes – Kesarwani, Taplin, Bartlett, O’Keefe, Blackaby, Lunaparra, Humbert, Ishii; Noes – None; Abstain – Tregub.",
